    "q-302235": {
      "dom_id": "step-q302235",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{8{x}^{6}+5}{2{x}^{5}-7x}=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{8{x}^{6}+5}{2{x}^{5}-7x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{8{x}^{6}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{7x}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(8x+\\frac{5}{{x}^{5}})}{(2-\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x+0}{2-0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,4x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
